  "id": "Compound::DB00696 - Gene::146",
  "verbalization": "Ergotamine is likely to interact with Adra1d through a shared mechanism involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor pathway. The evidence suggests that Ergotamine binds to Adra1b, which then participates in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately being participated by Adra1d. This implies that Ergotamine may exert its effects through a common pathway involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor, potentially modulating the activity of Adra1d. The overlapping involvement of Adra1b and Adra1d in the Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity suggests a possible functional relationship between these two receptors, although the exact nature of their interaction remains to be clarified. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the Alpha-adrenergic receptor in mediating Ergotamine's effects, with Adra1d possibly being a downstream effector in this process.",
